Antumbra: keep camera (V4L2) devices out of the Waydroid container.

Waydroid 1.6.3 bind-mounts every /dev/video* into the container and makes
them mode 0777 on every start, opening the cameras to every local user and
to every Android app (gated only by Android's own permission prompt).
Applied to Debian's waydroid 1.6.3+ds-2~bpo13+1 by
config/hooks/56-session-android.sh; the build fails if it does not apply.
Android's camera could not use the phone's raw CAMSS sensors anyway (its
external-camera HAL takes only MJPEG or depth streams), and config_3 also
denies the V4L2 major number (81) in the container's device cgroup.

--- a/usr/lib/waydroid/tools/actions/container_manager.py
+++ b/usr/lib/waydroid/tools/actions/container_manager.py
@@ -96,8 +96,8 @@
         perm_list.extend(glob.glob("/dev/dri/renderD*"))
         # Framebuffers
         perm_list.extend(glob.glob("/dev/fb*"))
-        # Videos
-        perm_list.extend(glob.glob("/dev/video*"))
+        # Antumbra: no camera (V4L2) devices: Waydroid would open them to
+        # every user (0777) and hand them to Android.
         # DMA-BUF Heaps
         perm_list.extend(glob.glob("/dev/dma_heap/*"))
 
--- a/usr/lib/waydroid/tools/helpers/lxc.py
+++ b/usr/lib/waydroid/tools/helpers/lxc.py
@@ -66,8 +66,7 @@
         make_entry(n)
     for n in glob.glob("/dev/graphics/fb*"):
         make_entry(n)
-    for n in glob.glob("/dev/video*"):
-        make_entry(n)
+    # Antumbra: no camera (V4L2) devices in the container.
     for n in glob.glob("/dev/dma_heap/*"):
         make_entry(n)
 
